# Sprint: Catalogue Item → Products Page Professional UI

## Overview
**Goal**: Audit and ensure professional Next.js 15 App Router architecture for the critical path: catalogue item click → products page display. Ensure semantic products are returned and logged to console.

**Current State**: 
- Semantic matching engine exists (`lib/catalogue/semanticMatching.ts`, `lib/catalogue/semanticConfig.ts`)
- DetailSection.tsx uses proper design system tokens
- Products page is async Server Component with parallel data fetching
- SidebarClient.tsx is the only Client Component in the flow

**Target State**:
- Semantic validation integrated into products fetch
- Console logging of semantic matches per category
- Zero regression in existing functionality
- Full adherence to Next.js 15 App Router patterns
- Design system compliance verified

---

## Audit Summary

### ✅ Architecture Compliance
| Checkpoint | Status | Evidence |
|------------|--------|----------|
| Server Components by default | ✅ | `page.tsx` exports async function, no "use client" |
| Parallel data fetching | ✅ | `Promise.all([getSelectedProducts(), getFilters...])` |
| No client-side navigation blocking | ✅ | Uses native `<a>` tags in DetailSection |
| Design system tokens | ✅ | `text-brand-400`, `text-secondary-300` etc. |
| Responsive breakpoints | ✅ | `xs:`, `sm:`, `lg-desktop:` used |

### ⚠️ Areas for Improvement
| Issue | Location | Severity |
|-------|----------|----------|
| Semantic validation not integrated | `getSelectedProducts.ts` | HIGH |
| No console logging of matches | `[...category]/page.tsx` | MEDIUM |
| Hardcoded colors in SidebarClient | `SidebarClient.tsx:18` | LOW |

### 🔴 Regression Risk Areas
1. `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts` - Core product query
2. `app/(store)/products/[...category]/page.tsx` - Category page
3. `app/(store)/products/page.tsx` - All products page
4. `app/components/layout/catalogue/details/DetailSection.tsx` - Navigation links
5. `lib/catalogue/semanticMatching.ts` - New semantic engine

---

## Scope Contract 1: Semantic Validation Integration

**Objective**: Integrate semantic matching into product fetch flow.

**Files to Modify**:
- `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts` - Add semantic validation wrapper

**Files to Create**:
- `lib/catalogue/semanticLogger.ts` - Console logging utilities

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] New function `getSelectedProductsWithValidation()` wraps existing function
- [ ] Semantic analysis runs on returned products
- [ ] Results include semantic match scores
- [ ] Console logging function exists with structured output

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] Validation runs after product fetch (non-blocking)
- [ ] Summary statistics calculated: valid (>=80), moderate (60-79), invalid (<60)
- [ ] Per-product results stored but don't affect return value
- [ ] Logging output has clear visual hierarchy

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Console output uses emojis: ✅ ⚠️ ❌
- [ ] Category context included in logs
- [ ] Product names truncated if too long (>40 chars)
- [ ] Summary shows match percentage

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] Validation only runs in development mode
- [ ] Errors in validation don't break product fetch
- [ ] Feature flag to disable: `DISABLE_SEMANTIC_VALIDATION`
- [ ] Performance: <10ms overhead per page load

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] Unit test: Validation returns same products as original function
- [ ] Unit test: Console logger formats output correctly
- [ ] Unit test: Error in validation is caught and logged
- [ ] E2E test: Category page still loads with products
- [ ] E2E test: Console shows semantic match output

---

## Scope Contract 2: Category Page Integration

**Objective**: Wire semantic validation into category page with console logging.

**Files to Modify**:
- `app/(store)/products/[...category]/page.tsx` - Add semantic logging

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] Page imports semantic validation function
- [ ] Page passes category slug to validation
- [ ] Console header logged: "=== Category: [Name] ==="

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] Logging happens after parallel data fetch
- [ ] Catalogue keys resolved and logged
- [ ] Product count logged before semantic analysis
- [ ] Summary statistics logged after analysis

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Category breadcrumb path included in logs
- [ ] Slug-to-ID resolution logged for debugging
- [ ] Empty categories show appropriate message
- [ ] Large product lists (>50) show summary only

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] Zero changes to page props or JSX
- [ ] No additional data fetching
- [ ] No impact on time-to-first-byte
- [ ] Async/await pattern preserved

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] E2E test: /products/headphones/open-back logs semantic matches
- [ ] E2E test: /products/audio-electronics/desktop-amps logs matches
- [ ] E2E test: /products/accessories/earpads logs matches
- [ ] Regression test: All existing E2E tests pass
- [ ] Performance test: Page load time <100ms increase

