## Sprint Execution Sequence

**Phase 1: Regression Safety (Day 1)**
1. Write regression tests (Scope Contract 4, Layers 1-2)
2. Run tests - verify they pass with current code
3. Create semantic logger utility (Scope Contract 1, Layer 1)
4. Implement console formatting (Scope Contract 1, Layer 2)

**Phase 2: Integration (Day 2)**
5. Integrate semantic validation into getSelectedProducts (Scope Contract 1, Layers 3-4)
6. Wire into category page (Scope Contract 2, Layers 1-2)
7. Add logging polish (Scope Contract 2, Layers 3-4)
8. Run regression tests - verify zero breakage

**Phase 3: Design System (Day 3)**
9. Audit SidebarClient for hardcoded colors (Scope Contract 3)
10. Fix any design system violations
11. Run visual regression tests
12. Manual QA on all 22 category pages

**Phase 4: Final Verification (Day 4)**
13. Full regression test run
14. Performance benchmark
15. Console output verification
16. Documentation update

---

## Success Criteria

**Functional**:
- [ ] Clicking any catalogue item navigates to correct products page
- [ ] Products displayed match category semantically (>=80 score)
- [ ] Console shows semantic match log with ✅ ⚠️ ❌ indicators
- [ ] All existing product fetch functionality works unchanged

**Performance**:
- [ ] Page load time increase <50ms
- [ ] Semantic validation overhead <10ms
- [ ] No memory leaks
- [ ] Lighthouse score unchanged

**Quality**:
- [ ] All regression tests pass
- [ ] All new unit tests pass
- [ ] All E2E tests pass
- [ ] No TypeScript errors
- [ ] No ESLint warnings
- [ ] No hardcoded colors

---

## Rollback Plan

If any critical issues arise:
1. Disable semantic validation via environment variable
2. Revert to `getSelectedProducts()` without wrapper
3. All existing functionality remains intact

---

